# {{ site.siteName }}

> Therapeutic counselling with {{ site.authorName }} — a warm, relational tradition of depth therapy that prioritises intimate human connection over clinical checklists. Sessions are held online over Zoom for clients across the United Kingdom, and the first session is free and no-commitment.

{{ site.authorName }} is a humanistic counsellor offering depth-oriented therapeutic counselling. The approach is present-moment and relational, inherited from a supervisor with over 30 years' experience in the existential-humanistic tradition founded by James Bugental. People commonly begin work around anxiety during major life change, loneliness or disconnection, dissatisfaction in significant relationships, recurring emotional patterns, or a search for greater meaning.

